WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.937
- [Mark] If there's something
strange in the neighborhood,

00:00:01.937 --> 00:00:02.770
- Who you gonna call?

00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:05.770
- [Mark] Well, with all due
respect to the Ghostbusters,

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:08.820
if I'm being attacked by
a spook, specter, ghost,

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:12.180
or a free-floating, full-torsoed,
vaporous apparition,

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:14.950
I'm not calling four
graduate school dropouts.

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:17.490
No, I'm either dialing up
the Winchester brothers

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:19.870
or I'm gassing up The Mystery Machine.

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:21.130
- Scooby and the gang.

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:23.673
These guys, they're our
freaking role models, man,

00:00:23.673 --> 00:00:25.550
except Fred, he's a wad.

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:27.840
Today it's "Scooby-Doo"
versus "Supernatural"

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.560
for the crown of the
all-time best battlers

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.360
of the bellowing blight.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:33.850
Scooby-Doo, Shaggy, and the gang

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:37.530
have been a worldwide institution
for generations of fans.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:40.430
Meanwhile, Sam and Dean
Winchester have cultivated

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:42.610
an impressive 15-year run,

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:45.238
thanks to a legion of die-hard supporters.

00:00:45.238 --> 00:00:47.919
Whether the enemy du jour
is ghosts, werewolves,

00:00:47.919 --> 00:00:51.040
or Mr. Withers, who runs
the old amusement park,

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:53.010
these two teams of lovable underdogs

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:55.000
always get the job done.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.727
But what happens when they
face off against each other?

00:00:57.727 --> 00:00:58.990
Zoinks!

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:00.560
Here's how we'll determine a winner.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.230
Round one, Tomatometer.

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:03.884
Round two, popularity.

00:01:03.884 --> 00:01:05.990
Round three, characters.

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:07.930
And then we'll do a wild card round

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:09.950
to settle the score once and for all.

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:12.007
I'll then say goodnight,
then it's up to you,

00:01:12.007 --> 00:01:13.912
the home viewer, to cast your vote.

00:01:13.912 --> 00:01:16.367
The mystery gang is taking
on the Winchester family

00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:19.063
and a whole box of Scooby
Snacks are on the line.

00:01:19.063 --> 00:01:21.730
I once ate a Milk-Bone on a dare.

00:01:21.730 --> 00:01:22.563
Let's get it on!

00:01:22.563 --> 00:01:25.442
- The most beautiful words in the world!

00:01:25.442 --> 00:01:27.404
All you can eat.

00:01:27.404 --> 00:01:30.093
- Clear eyes and the clogged
arteries, can't lose.

00:01:30.093 --> 00:01:32.138
- [Mark] Round one: Tomatometer.

00:01:32.138 --> 00:01:34.610
Everyone, and their mother,
and their grandmother,

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:37.350
and their great-grandma's ghost
has heard of "Scooby-Doo,"

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:39.500
and "Supernatural" has
enough hardcore fans

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.410
to populate an entire country.

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:42.820
But how do the critics feel

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:44.931
about these celebrated franchises?

00:01:44.931 --> 00:01:47.240
- Pull my finger, uh-oh, too late!

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.030
- [Mark] Okay, Winchesters,
y'all wanna take a crack

00:01:49.030 --> 00:01:50.190
at this one first?

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:52.770
The boys and their gaggle
of relatives, friends,

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:56.300
and spooky enemies appear to
be BFFS with the Tomatometer.

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:58.420
But whether you've never
heard of "Supernatural"

00:01:58.420 --> 00:01:59.820
or you're a hardcore fan,

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:01.350
you're gonna need to brace yourself

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:05.503
because the show has an
overall average of 93 percent.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:08.033
- What?

00:02:08.033 --> 00:02:09.090
- [Mark] And that's not
like out of a thousand,

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:11.860
that's out of a hundred,
that's an A average, kids!

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:14.710
The show's lowest season
was scored at 63 percent,

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:17.010
which is still Fresh,
and the show can boast

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:20.050
multiple perfect seasons at 100 percent,

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:23.550
including its currently
ongoing 15th season.

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:25.839
Wait, so the current
season is still perfect?

00:02:25.839 --> 00:02:28.070
Okay, nobody talk to it in the dugout.

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:30.250
Leave it alone, do not jinx this.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.970
- We got work to do.

00:02:31.970 --> 00:02:32.947
- [Mark] You may be saying to yourself,

00:02:32.947 --> 00:02:35.657
"Okay, Mark, you handsome hunk of granite,

00:02:35.657 --> 00:02:39.061
"93 percent is good, but
'Scooby-Doo' is beloved."

00:02:39.061 --> 00:02:39.936
Right?

00:02:39.936 --> 00:02:42.650
Well, not necessarily by the critics.

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:44.140
So we don't have Tomatometer scores

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:46.800
for the original CBS or
ABC runs of the show,

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:49.180
but we do have them for
the more recent live-action

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:52.430
and animated features, and
it only averages 50 percent.

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:53.930
50 percent?

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:56.340
In what twisted world
could you possibly rate

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:58.929
a ghost-fighting dog Rotten?

00:02:58.929 --> 00:03:01.480
Despite sizeable box office success,

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.060
it appears the live-action films

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:05.180
starring Matthew Lillard,
Linda Cardellini,

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:07.950
Sarah Michelle Gellar, and
my close personal friend,

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:10.500
Freddie Prinze Jr, are considered Rotten!

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.930
They average just 26 percent.

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:15.700
However, a handful of the
animated films are Fresh,

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:18.060
with "Scooby-Doo on Zombie Island"

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:21.620
taking the top franchise
score at 86 percent.

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:23.120
And that movie came out, like, a decade

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:25.110
before "The Walking Dead," so Scooby,

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:26.349
you were ahead of the curve.

00:03:26.349 --> 00:03:28.649
♪ Do you hear the screeching of an owl ♪

00:03:28.649 --> 00:03:30.430
♪ Do you hear the wind begin ♪

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:31.990
- [Mark] So despite the
mystery gang's good looks

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:34.110
and sense of humor, it's the other sect

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:36.617
of funny hunks that's gonna
take round number one.

00:03:36.617 --> 00:03:38.970
"Supernatural" has a good
enough Tomatometer score

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:40.720
to get into an Ivy League school,

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:44.277
and that's why it's going
up one-nothing on Scooby.

00:03:44.277 --> 00:03:47.654
♪ Eye of the tiger, it's
the thrill of the fight ♪

00:03:47.654 --> 00:03:49.310
♪ Rising up ♪

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:50.903
- [Mark] Round two: popularity.

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:53.550
To all the kids out there watching,

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:55.340
being popular, it's not a big deal.

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:58.160
Follow your own path, march to
the beat of your own drummer.

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:00.510
Unless, of course, you're
trying to win a round

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:04.410
of this show, then being cool
and lovable really helps.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.730
- Keeping it real.

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:07.470
- [Mark] I mentioned the
mystery team's foibles

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:10.010
as it pertains to critics
on the Tomatometer,

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:11.290
but Scooby does rebound

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:13.670
when it comes to the audience score.

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:16.430
Him and the gang make it
into Fresh territory, barely,

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:18.140
at 62 percent.

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:21.049
However, "Supernatural" continues
its sterling Fresh record

00:04:21.049 --> 00:04:24.690
with a healthy B average of 86 percent.

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:27.030
And, according to the
audience, between seasons three

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:29.190
and five of the show,
"Supernatural" enjoyed

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:32.200
a three-year high of 95 percent.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.970
Meanwhile, the two series,
"What's New, Scooby-Doo?"

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:37.410
and "Shaggy &amp; Scooby-Doo Get a Clue!"

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:39.416
each have a perfect 100 percent,

00:04:39.416 --> 00:04:43.920
although 2018's "Daphne &amp;
Velma" only garnered 37 percent.

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:45.370
Why is that so low?

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:47.880
I like "Daphne &amp; Velma,"
did Scrappy-Doo show up

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:49.190
and ruin it?

00:04:49.190 --> 00:04:51.200
More on you in the next round, ugh.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:52.570
- People adore me!

00:04:52.570 --> 00:04:54.790
- Popularity can also be
determined by a question

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:57.360
as simple as, "Does
anyone watch your show?"

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:59.508
Sam, Dean, and the gang
certainly have solid ratings

00:04:59.508 --> 00:05:00.990
that strengthen their case.

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:03.080
For the first 14 seasons
of "Supernatural,"

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:06.590
it averaged 2.35 million
viewers per episode,

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:08.360
and that's all the more
impressive considering

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:10.280
it originally aired on The CW,

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:12.360
and not one of the major networks.

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:14.143
Fans were onboard with the
brothers from the start

00:05:14.143 --> 00:05:18.490
as season one set a show
record of 3.81 million viewers

00:05:18.490 --> 00:05:19.323
per week.

00:05:19.323 --> 00:05:21.970
However, many more fans, like yours truly,

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:24.602
didn't really discover the
greatness of "Supernatural"

00:05:24.602 --> 00:05:28.346
until it was available on
streaming platforms like Netflix.

00:05:28.346 --> 00:05:30.680
As a matter of fact, I think
the first time I saw it,

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:34.930
I had a DVD mailed to me by Netflix.

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:36.417
I miss the medieval times.

00:05:36.417 --> 00:05:38.144
- Our one chance!

00:05:38.144 --> 00:05:39.060
- Isn't that the speech from--

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:40.057
- It's the only one he knows.

00:05:40.057 --> 00:05:42.450
- [Mark] "Scooby-Doo"
obviously goes way further back

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:44.610
into human and dog history.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.810
The show debuted in 1969

00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:49.200
and has been in the public
consciousness ever since.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.360
And even though the ratings

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:52.370
for all the various
incarnations of "Scooby"

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:53.540
are murky at best,

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:58.170
I can report that in 1969,
65 percent of households

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:00.810
were tuned into CBS on Saturday morning,

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:02.370
where it originally aired.

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:04.890
That's gonna sell a lot of
Anacin and talcum powder.

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:05.723
- Scooby-Doo!

00:06:06.727 --> 00:06:07.990
- [Mark] "Scooby" does have the advantage

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:09.600
of having been on the big screen,

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:12.090
churning out two live-action hits early on

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:13.177
in this millennium.

00:06:13.177 --> 00:06:15.730
"Scooby-Doo" and its sequel,
"Monsters Unleashed,"

00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:19.460
combined for an impressive 384
million dollars domestically

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:22.173
and 740 million dollars worldwide.

00:06:22.173 --> 00:06:25.680
Apparently people love dogs
and their stoned owners.

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:26.904
Furthering the case
for The Mystery Machine

00:06:26.904 --> 00:06:29.450
is the Cartoon Network phenomenon.

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:32.300
Check this, "Scooby-Doo! The
Mystery Begins" premiered

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:36.380
in 2009 and broke virtually
every record that channel had.

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:38.370
It got 6 million viewers!

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:39.897
Then, the next year, its follow-up,

00:06:39.897 --> 00:06:43.540
"Curse of the Lake Monster,"
garnered 5 million views.

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:46.290
Both were good for the number
one telecast of the year

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:47.450
on Cartoon Network.

00:06:47.450 --> 00:06:49.020
Sure, it's a bit of a lopsided battle,

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:51.060
having a TV show battle another TV show

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:53.417
that also has movies, but
maybe there is a reason

00:06:53.417 --> 00:06:56.170
"Scooby" got to be on the silver
screen in the first place.

00:06:56.170 --> 00:06:58.182
But before I give up on the
Winchesters in this round,

00:06:58.182 --> 00:07:01.170
let's see how many episodes they've made.

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:02.200
Uh, wow, really?

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:05.440
327 "Supernatural" shows
will have been made

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:06.640
by the end of the run.

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:09.240
I've never done 327 of
anything in my life.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:10.550
Well, that one thing.

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:11.510
- Dude.

00:07:11.510 --> 00:07:12.820
Were you on my computer?

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:14.037
- Other than that, but look,

00:07:14.037 --> 00:07:16.050
"Scooby-Doo" can even
top that gaudy number,

00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:20.390
because his gang has 376
episodes over 16 different shows,

00:07:20.390 --> 00:07:23.600
five animated TV films, two
theatrically released movies,

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:27.427
42 animated direct-to-DVD films,
six direct-to-DVD specials,

00:07:27.427 --> 00:07:30.620
three direct-to-DVD live-action
movies, 35 web shorts,

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:31.924
537 comic book issues,

00:07:31.924 --> 00:07:33.480
(sighing)

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:34.313
okay.

00:07:34.313 --> 00:07:35.146
We get the point.

00:07:35.146 --> 00:07:37.230
Scooby's popular, and he gets a snack,

00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:40.196
because his squad wins round number two.

00:07:40.196 --> 00:07:41.927
Scooby

00:07:41.927 --> 00:07:42.780
dooby

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:44.320
doo!

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:46.480
- [Mark] Round three: characters.

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:49.500
So many legendary starred
characters and role-players

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:52.480
to consider here, I might
need more time to think.

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:53.750
- I don't know, gang.

00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:56.150
Sounds like this could be
the start of a mystery.

00:07:56.150 --> 00:07:57.590
- [Mark] Okay, so where do we begin?

00:07:57.590 --> 00:07:59.760
Let's get the core
starters involved first.

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:02.100
Sam, Dean, you guys are up.

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:03.860
Jared Padalecki and Jensen Ackles

00:08:03.860 --> 00:08:05.720
have the kind of chemistry that scientists

00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:07.290
in lab coats crave.

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:08.770
They play off each other so well

00:08:08.770 --> 00:08:10.757
even when they're having
fun introducing themselves

00:08:10.757 --> 00:08:13.494
under any of their myriad pseudonyms.

00:08:13.494 --> 00:08:16.150
- I'm Dean Winchester, I'm
looking for the Devil's son,

00:08:16.150 --> 00:08:17.253
this badge is fake.

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:20.360
- [Mark] They even used fake monikers

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:22.277
referencing Van Halen and Metallica,

00:08:22.277 --> 00:08:25.590
so you know that's an easy
early point for "Supernatural"

00:08:25.590 --> 00:08:26.423
in this round.

00:08:26.423 --> 00:08:27.830
Whether it's their powerful bro-hugs,

00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:30.390
their willingness to sacrifice
themselves for each other,

00:08:30.390 --> 00:08:32.096
or just karaoke perfection,

00:08:32.096 --> 00:08:34.390
♪ Straightenin' the curves ♪

00:08:34.390 --> 00:08:36.930
- [Mark] Sam and Dean make
for amazingly sturdy anchors

00:08:36.930 --> 00:08:37.763
of the show.

00:08:37.763 --> 00:08:39.059
♪ I'm wanted ♪

00:08:39.059 --> 00:08:40.800
♪ Wanted ♪

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:42.951
- [Mark] But Scooby-Doo
and Shaggy are icons.

00:08:42.951 --> 00:08:44.880
They debuted in the Summer of Love,

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:46.310
and audiences all over the world

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:48.037
have been swooned ever since.

00:08:48.037 --> 00:08:50.460
Scooby's plucky optimism meshes so well

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:52.290
with Shaggy's fearful reluctance,

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:54.140
and the two always meet in the middle

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:56.361
with their common love of food.

00:08:56.361 --> 00:08:58.430
(quirky music)
(sniffing)

00:08:58.430 --> 00:08:59.340
(sighing)

00:08:59.340 --> 00:09:00.610
But let's not forget the other trio

00:09:00.610 --> 00:09:03.110
who spent decades in the
hallowed Mystery Machine:

00:09:03.110 --> 00:09:05.260
Fred, Velma, and Daphne.

00:09:05.260 --> 00:09:07.330
Fred takes his role of
being a nerd do-good-er

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:09.600
dressed like a preppy frat boy in stride,

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:11.197
and he loves splitting up.

00:09:11.197 --> 00:09:13.570
It's like his favorite pastime.

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:15.640
Daphne and Velma, when
their unique abilities

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:17.730
as amateur detectives, and, all told,

00:09:17.730 --> 00:09:22.730
the gang has rounded up a
grand total of 392 villains.

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:23.870
Yeah, I counted.

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:26.257
I, I have that kind of
free time these days.

00:09:26.257 --> 00:09:29.500
"Supernatural" has also had a
blast introducing characters

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:31.930
who expanded from
becoming mere role-players

00:09:31.930 --> 00:09:34.410
into regularly occurring cast members.

00:09:34.410 --> 00:09:37.040
How about Castiel's
entrance in season four?

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:38.540
- Hey, ass-butt.

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:40.370
- [Mark] Mary Winchester
and John Winchester

00:09:40.370 --> 00:09:43.170
also factor prominently, and
the show is further bolstered

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:45.695
by memorable turns from
famous people like Felicia Day

00:09:45.695 --> 00:09:47.400
and Sterling K. Brown.

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:50.402
Then you have the characters
that surround the mystery gang.

00:09:50.402 --> 00:09:53.490
(sighs) Okay, here's the good news, first.

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:55.830
Memorable cameos had been
a staple of "Scooby-Doo"

00:09:55.830 --> 00:09:57.060
since the beginning.

00:09:57.060 --> 00:09:59.700
Everyone from The Monkees to Mama Cass

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:02.150
to the Harlem Globetrotters
have enjoyed the company

00:10:02.150 --> 00:10:03.708
of Scooby and Norville.

00:10:03.708 --> 00:10:06.340
Did you know that was, that
was Shaggy's real name, was,

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:07.470
was Norville?

00:10:07.470 --> 00:10:09.358
I'd probably go by Shaggy too.

00:10:09.358 --> 00:10:11.730
But look, I can't let the
mystery gang off the hook

00:10:11.730 --> 00:10:13.920
that easy, there's an
elephant in the room,

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:15.658
and it's Scooby's nephew.

00:10:15.658 --> 00:10:17.678
- Scrappy dappy doo!

00:10:17.678 --> 00:10:19.244
- [Mark] To put it gently,

00:10:19.244 --> 00:10:21.000
not well-liked.

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:23.620
I myself have a confounding
relationship with Scrappy

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:25.600
because, as a kid, I thought he was great,

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:27.507
he was maybe my favorite
character on the show.

00:10:27.507 --> 00:10:30.490
And then, you know, I became an adult,

00:10:30.490 --> 00:10:34.470
and, the thing is, seeing
"Scooby-Doo" as an adult,

00:10:34.470 --> 00:10:36.427
I watched the show and I was saying,

00:10:36.427 --> 00:10:38.867
"Scrappy is the most annoying character

00:10:38.867 --> 00:10:40.550
"I've ever seen in my life."

00:10:40.550 --> 00:10:43.403
It's hard to make me not like a dog!

00:10:43.403 --> 00:10:45.870
It's like Scrappy-Doo
and what other hated dog

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:47.030
is there, ever?

00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:49.310
I was even cool with
Poochie from "The Simpsons."

00:10:49.310 --> 00:10:51.200
The Taco Bell chihuahua, sure.

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:53.290
Scrappy-Doo, no thank you.

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:55.370
There was also a
Scooby-Dum and a Dooby-Doo,

00:10:55.370 --> 00:10:58.260
which I'm pretty sure
Shaggy tried to smoke.

00:10:58.260 --> 00:10:59.730
Overall, it's a tough call here,

00:10:59.730 --> 00:11:02.077
but there's no contest
in terms of role-players.

00:11:02.077 --> 00:11:05.040
"Supernatural" has solid
contributors coming off the bench

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:08.433
every season, and they
never had a Scrappy-Doo.

00:11:08.433 --> 00:11:11.690
I'm trying to think of any
other dog that I disliked.

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:13.810
Even the replacement Brian on "Family Guy"

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:16.144
at least had a funny line here or there.

00:11:16.144 --> 00:11:19.840
But if we're looking at
a truly iconic core cast,

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:21.459
you can't ignore the staying power

00:11:21.459 --> 00:11:26.120
of Fred, Daphne, Velma,
Shaggy, and, of course, Scooby.

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:27.720
They're underrated as detectives,

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:30.170
and even if they aren't
as cool as Sam and Dean,

00:11:30.170 --> 00:11:32.240
they're endlessly entertaining to watch.

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:34.800
In the tightest round yet,
I'm gonna give the win

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:38.073
to Scooby and the gang,
and they're up two to one.

00:11:38.073 --> 00:11:42.323
♪ This is how we solve the mystery ♪

00:11:43.912 --> 00:11:44.745
Bye.

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:48.101
- [Mark] Wild card round: villains.

00:11:48.101 --> 00:11:49.430
Okay, I know what you're thinking,

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:51.980
Mark, don't villains
just count as characters?

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:53.890
Technically yes, but the big baddies

00:11:53.890 --> 00:11:56.400
are such an integral part of both shows

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:58.047
that they deserve their own category.

00:11:58.047 --> 00:12:00.297
(whooping)

00:12:01.895 --> 00:12:03.330
- That was scary!

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:04.710
- [Mark] The name of
the show "Supernatural"

00:12:04.710 --> 00:12:05.600
says it all.

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:08.520
You got your classic ghosts
and ghouls, vampires,

00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:10.884
werewolves, but there's
also really freaky stuff

00:12:10.884 --> 00:12:13.850
that I'm glad I never heard
of when I was a child.

00:12:13.850 --> 00:12:15.868
How about the darkness?

00:12:15.868 --> 00:12:17.495
No, this is not "The Thing Called Love,"

00:12:17.495 --> 00:12:20.450
in fact, it's the older sister of God.

00:12:20.450 --> 00:12:21.770
Yeah, of God!

00:12:21.770 --> 00:12:24.350
And she ain't happy her little
bro gets all the credit.

00:12:24.350 --> 00:12:25.930
You got the horsemen of the apocalypse,

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:28.860
leviathans, djinns, who
I actually had heard of

00:12:28.860 --> 00:12:31.000
thanks to Magic: The Gathering.

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:33.140
What's really cool about each
villain that they take on

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:34.810
is the backstory that we get.

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:37.640
The nod to mythology is one
of the most intriguing aspects

00:12:37.640 --> 00:12:38.730
of "Supernatural."

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:41.090
You get the siren or the crocotta,

00:12:41.090 --> 00:12:44.310
which mimics human voices
to draw in its prey.

00:12:44.310 --> 00:12:46.370
And this isn't to mention
all the other demons,

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:48.610
you got your changelings,
you got your hell hounds,

00:12:48.610 --> 00:12:50.700
the Winchesters have had
to deal with these things

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:52.277
on a regular basis.

00:12:52.277 --> 00:12:54.830
- Listen, Velma, this
isn't the Scooby gang.

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:56.770
- [Mark] So how does "Scooby-Doo" answer?

00:12:56.770 --> 00:12:58.230
Well, look, you may think "Scooby-Doo"

00:12:58.230 --> 00:12:59.530
is just a kid-friendly show,

00:12:59.530 --> 00:13:01.650
but listen to this roster of baddies.

00:13:01.650 --> 00:13:05.630
Apeman, viking ghost, no-faced
zombie, phantom virus!

00:13:05.630 --> 00:13:07.291
Hey, that's topical.

00:13:07.291 --> 00:13:10.360
And you also had your
sillier variety like Catman,

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:12.260
ghost clown, the Loch Ness Monster,

00:13:12.260 --> 00:13:15.260
which actually turned
out to be a vehicle, eh.

00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:17.750
The big obstacle the mystery
gang faces in this round

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:19.837
is the lack of a recurring threat.

00:13:19.837 --> 00:13:21.978
"Supernatural" had some all-time baddies

00:13:21.978 --> 00:13:23.670
coming back for more.

00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:26.550
Crowley vacillated between
villain and anti-hero

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:28.950
but was always a captivating watch.

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:30.820
And Lilith eventually reached her goal

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:34.080
of destroying the 66 locks
keeping Lucifer at bay.

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:36.540
And Lucifer himself, well,
as you might imagine,

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:38.130
he tortured poor Sam so much,

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:39.730
he had to go to the psych ward!

00:13:39.730 --> 00:13:41.870
The only real counter
"Scooby" has in this round

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:46.040
is if we, the audience, can
consider Scrappy-Doo a villain.

00:13:46.040 --> 00:13:47.630
I think a lot of people out there would.

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:51.010
He's certainly a show ruiner,
but he did try his best.

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:52.700
Okay, fine, Scrappy, you're not a villain,

00:13:52.700 --> 00:13:54.690
but you're just super annoying.

00:13:54.690 --> 00:13:56.420
The reason I respect both squads

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:59.580
of demon-deflecting detectives
is their continued ability

00:13:59.580 --> 00:14:01.930
to take on cases no one else would.

00:14:01.930 --> 00:14:04.820
Most humans and-or canines
would be too afraid

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:06.490
to battle any of these creatures,

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:09.217
and that's only if they even
believed in them at all.

00:14:09.217 --> 00:14:11.760
- I'm gonna go stop the big bad wolf,

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:13.560
which is the weirdest
thing I've ever said.

00:14:13.560 --> 00:14:16.280
- [Mark] The mystery gang and
the Winchesters had the faith

00:14:16.280 --> 00:14:19.553
to fight the scariest things
on Earth or elsewhere.

00:14:19.553 --> 00:14:21.570
The big difference is that Scooby's team

00:14:21.570 --> 00:14:24.192
usually found out the big
scary thing they were facing

00:14:24.192 --> 00:14:26.590
was just some old town kook,

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:27.930
some older fella who didn't like

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:30.420
the last meal government
cheese the city served him

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:32.120
and so he decided to get revenge,

00:14:32.120 --> 00:14:33.450
and he would have gotten away with it,

00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:35.530
if it wasn't for you meddling kids!

00:14:35.530 --> 00:14:36.930
- Hey, we're not kids!

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:39.810
- The meddlesome kids named Sam
and Dean, on the other hand,

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:42.980
they fought the scariest
actual villains imaginable,

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:45.663
and that's why they get the
win in the wild card round.

00:14:45.663 --> 00:14:48.580
The Winchesters take it,
and it's all tied up at two.

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:49.863
- You know what?

00:14:52.346 --> 00:14:53.600
You're awesome.

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:55.950
- And now we're at the
point in the show where I,

00:14:55.950 --> 00:14:58.300
your fearless host,
has to render a verdict

00:14:58.300 --> 00:14:59.800
and break this tie.

00:14:59.800 --> 00:15:00.710
But first, did you know

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:03.970
about the legendary cross-over-ish
episode of "Supernatural"

00:15:03.970 --> 00:15:05.880
that involves Scooby-Doo and his team?

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:06.940
(exclaiming)

00:15:06.940 --> 00:15:08.448
- You're a cartoon!
- You're a cartoon!

00:15:08.448 --> 00:15:09.500
- I'm a cartoon!
- I'm a cartoon!

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:11.470
- [Mark] They call it the
"Scoobynatural" episode

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:13.670
and one of the many highlights
is that we get to see

00:15:13.670 --> 00:15:17.350
sort of a showdown between
two celebrated vehicles.

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:20.030
So the Winchesters, they
have their '67 Chevelle,

00:15:20.030 --> 00:15:21.990
it's a classic, and if you're a gear-head,

00:15:21.990 --> 00:15:24.370
you know that thing can
pack some serious punch.

00:15:24.370 --> 00:15:28.340
But it actually gets outran
by The Mystery Machine

00:15:28.340 --> 00:15:29.670
in that episode.

00:15:29.670 --> 00:15:32.640
So maybe the van was powered
by unwavering optimism

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:35.880
or a nitrous oxide boost,
but it did win the race.

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:38.776
So is that enough to give
"Scooby-Doo" the win today?

00:15:38.776 --> 00:15:40.930
Okay, look, both teams
deserve our respect.

00:15:40.930 --> 00:15:43.590
They've outlasted countless
witches and ghosts

00:15:43.590 --> 00:15:46.270
and the most ridiculous
monsters you could think of.

00:15:46.270 --> 00:15:49.170
And they managed to
entertain us consistently

00:15:49.170 --> 00:15:50.270
in the process.

00:15:50.270 --> 00:15:52.700
They're both titans of the
world of the supernatural,

00:15:52.700 --> 00:15:56.640
but only one can be called truly iconic.

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:58.820
Scooby-Doo and his pals
have been crushing the game

00:15:58.820 --> 00:16:00.130
for more than 50 years,

00:16:00.130 --> 00:16:01.123
and they've entertained us all

00:16:01.123 --> 00:16:03.570
from the time we were wee little tykes,

00:16:03.570 --> 00:16:05.720
all the way through our adult years.

00:16:05.720 --> 00:16:08.740
In a recent survey,
Ranker listed Scooby-Doo

00:16:08.740 --> 00:16:12.886
as the number one greatest
cartoon character in history!

00:16:12.886 --> 00:16:14.850
Now, I'm a fan of Sam and Dean,

00:16:14.850 --> 00:16:17.270
but could they have taken
down the likes of Bugs Bunny

00:16:17.270 --> 00:16:19.090
or Homer Simpson?

00:16:19.090 --> 00:16:20.359
I don't think so.

00:16:20.359 --> 00:16:23.060
I think even hardcore
defenders of "Supernatural"

00:16:23.060 --> 00:16:25.570
will admit that we all
owe a tip of the cap

00:16:25.570 --> 00:16:28.960
or a tug of the ascot to the mystery gang.

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:30.110
- Take a bullet for that dog.

00:16:30.110 --> 00:16:31.680
- Without them, generations of kids

00:16:31.680 --> 00:16:34.460
may never have gotten as
invested in supernatural lore,

00:16:34.460 --> 00:16:37.160
and who knows if any of
these other shows or movies

00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:38.750
that we take for granted today

00:16:38.750 --> 00:16:39.850
would have gotten made.

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:40.960
- Hey, did you believe me when I said

00:16:40.960 --> 00:16:42.860
I thought we could win this thing?

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:43.693
No?

00:16:43.693 --> 00:16:45.194
- Hold the phone.

00:16:45.194 --> 00:16:46.027
- Jeepers.

00:16:46.027 --> 00:16:46.988
- Jinkies.

00:16:46.988 --> 00:16:47.821
- Zoinks?

00:16:47.821 --> 00:16:49.850
- Okay, so "Scooby-Doo" gets the win,

00:16:49.850 --> 00:16:52.290
but that's just our
opinion, now it's your turn,

00:16:52.290 --> 00:16:54.564
head to the comments right
now and vote for who you think

00:16:54.564 --> 00:16:59.564
is the best supernatural
poltergeist babblers of all time.

00:16:59.730 --> 00:17:02.220
Okay, we're gonna say
goodnight to everybody.

00:17:02.220 --> 00:17:03.520
Keep wearing those ascots.

00:17:04.370 --> 00:17:06.591
Somebody wants a Scooby Snack.

00:17:06.591 --> 00:17:09.817
We'll see you next time here on the show.

00:17:09.817 --> 00:17:11.831
Like, zoinks, Scoob!

00:17:11.831 --> 00:17:14.414
(upbeat music)

